# REQUIRES: verilator
# vmem-rings: a virtual memory's per-instance read buffer as a fixed ring. The
# memory's answers are written to an image (a second virtual memory, a row per
# instance); a lead before each instance's next first use, a prefetch reads its
# row into entry instance mod R of a ring of R entries, R set by the schedule's
# window. Sixteen leaves (a class of 16 instances, a read held when bit 1 is
# low, read first), against a model of both controllers (Inputs/tb_vmem_ring.sv):
# the static simulator matches the target at any answer latency, with stalled
# channels, controllers out of room and bubbles; with rings of 16, 8 and 4
# entries (shared by 1, 2 and 4 instances), nested sequencers, a short lead.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/vmemring
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/l2 --static --virtual-memories ram --vmem-rings 2 Leaf 2> %t/l2.log > /dev/null
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=L2 < %t/l2.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VH < %t/l2/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MLIR < %t/l2/foldsim_sim.mlir
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -DIW1=4 -Mdir %t/l2/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem_ring.sv top.sv %t/l2/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/l2/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/l2/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+1 +lo=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/l2/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+2 +lo=1 +hi=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/l2/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+3 +lo=20 +hi=200 +full=50 +stall=10 | FileCheck %s
# The image's answers fast and the memory's slow: a prefetch must wait for its
# instance's answer (a prefetch that does not reads a stale image row).
# RUN: %t/l2/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+12 +lo=40 +hi=200 +lo1=1 +hi1=2 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/l2/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+13 +lo=1 +hi=100 +lo1=1 +hi1=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/l1 --static --virtual-memories ram --vmem-rings 1 Leaf 2> %t/l1.log > /dev/null
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=L1 < %t/l1.log
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -DIW1=4 -Mdir %t/l1/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem_ring.sv top.sv %t/l1/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/l1/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/l1/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+4 +lo=5 +hi=60 +full=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/l8 --static --virtual-memories ram --vmem-rings 8 Leaf 2> %t/l8.log > /dev/null
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=L8 < %t/l8.log
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -DIW1=6 -Mdir %t/l8/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem_ring.sv top.sv %t/l8/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/l8/build.log 2>&1
# The lead covers a one-host-cycle answer: H stays II (22).
# RUN: %t/l8/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+5 +lo=1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FAST
# RUN: %t/l8/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+6 +lo=5 +hi=60 +full=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# Controllers whose requests wait in a FIFO of 8 entries drained slowly (a
# group member's, `free` twice its free entries): the image's requests (a
# prefetch's read and an answer's write, rarely in one host cycle) leave only
# within its room. Before, the answers' writes left as they came and the FIFO
# overflowed (PROTOCOL) at drain 40 and 25.
# RUN: %t/l8/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+14 +lo=1 +fifo=8 +drain=40 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/l8/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+15 +lo=1 +fifo=8 +drain=25 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/l8/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+16 +lo=40 +hi=200 +lo1=1 +hi1=2 +fifo=8 +drain=50 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/m40 --static --modulo --min-ii 40 --virtual-memories ram --vmem-rings 6 Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -DIW1=5 -Mdir %t/m40/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem_ring.sv top.sv %t/m40/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/m40/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/m40/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+7 +lo=5 +hi=60 +full=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/nest --static --virtual-memories ram --vmem-rings 3 --nest Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -DIW1=5 -Mdir %t/nest/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem_ring.sv top.sv %t/nest/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/nest/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/nest/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+8 +lo=1 +hi=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/short --static --virtual-memories ram --vmem-rings 3 --short-lead Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -DIW1=5 -Mdir %t/short/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem_ring.sv top.sv %t/short/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/short/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/short/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+9 +lo=1 +hi=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/bub --static --virtual-memories ram --vmem-rings 3 --bubbles --nest Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -DIW1=5 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/bub/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem_ring.sv top.sv %t/bub/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/bub/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/bub/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+10 +lo=5 +hi=60 +full=30 +bubble=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/bub/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+11 +lo=20 +hi=200 +full=50 +bubble=60 +burst=8 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/bub/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+17 +lo=1 +fifo=8 +drain=25 +bubble=30 | FileCheck %s
# A cap below the window keeps the buffers (and the simulator as without rings).
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/cap --static --virtual-memories ram --vmem-rings 8 --vmem-ring-entries 4 Leaf 2> %t/cap.log > /dev/null
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CAP < %t/cap.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CAPVH < %t/cap/foldsim_sim.vh
# L2: vmem-rings: Leaf: 1 read buffers as rings of 4 entries (window 4, 16 instances, 16 prefetches a frame, lead 2)
# L1: vmem-rings: Leaf: 1 read buffers as rings of 4 entries (window 3, 16 instances, 16 prefetches a frame, lead 1)
# L8: vmem-rings: Leaf: 1 read buffers as rings of 16 entries (window 9, 16 instances, 16 prefetches a frame, lead 8)
# CAP: vmem-rings: Leaf: read buffers kept (more than 4 entries (a window of 9))
# The memory and its image (16 instances x 1 row).
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_COUNT 2
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_AW 4
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_INSTANCES 16
# The image: tags {write, entry} over instance 0, a row per instance.
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_1_IW 4
# VH-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_1_AW 4
# VH-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_1_DW 8
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_1_INSTANCES 1
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_1_TAGW 3
# CAPVH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_COUNT 1
# No per-instance buffer: a ring of 4 entries, filled by the image's answers,
# the queue of prefetches waiting for their instances' reads ({instance, entry})
# and the queue of the answers' image writes ({instance, data}).
# MLIR-NOT: ram_rdata = seq.firmem
# MLIR: %ram_ring = seq.firmem 0, 1, undefined, undefined : <4 x 8, mask 1>
# MLIR: seq.firmem.write_port %ram_ring[{{.*}}] = %vm1_rsp_data, clock %hostClock enable %vm1_rsp_valid
# MLIR: %ram_ring_flight_queue = seq.firmem 0, 1, undefined, undefined : <64 x 6, mask 1>
# MLIR: %ram_ring_flight_writes = seq.firmem 0, 1, undefined, undefined : <32 x 12, mask 1>
# The entry read combinationally into a register whose synchronous reset is the skip (a use whose prefetch would
# have come before the first frame reads zero): no select on the data.
# MLIR: %ram_ring_data = seq.firreg %{{.*}} clock %hostClock reset sync %ram_ring_skip2, %c0_i8
# MLIR-NOT: ram_ring_skip1
# A prefetch's entry, its rank in the frame's prefetches mod R, is counted from the frame's first position (no table).
# MLIR: %ram_ring_prank = seq.firreg
# FAST: {{^}}MATCH 196 cycles in 4400 host cycles, H 22.00
# CHECK: {{^}}MATCH
